e coordination.\n- Other moves like P: f7-f5 or P: g7-g5 push pawns but ignore the hanging bishop.\n\nThe most forcing and advantageous move is **B: f3-g2**, capturing the bishop. If White recaptures with Kxg2, their king is exposed and loses castling rights (though already moved, so irrelevant), but more importantly, I gain a lead in development and open lines for my rook on h8.\n\nReason: Capturing the bishop on g2 is a winning trade: it removes a key defender of White’s king, gains material (equal pieces but better timing), and disrupts White’s position. It also opens the g-file for potential rook pressure. There is no immediate counterattack from White after Bxg2.\n\nAnswer: B: f3-g2"}
