ing, forces a response, and may win material or disrupt white’s coordination.]\n\nReason: [Delivering check with the queen to e5 maximizes pressure on white’s biggest weakness — the centrally stranded king. It cannot be ignored, and white must respond (likely by moving the king or blocking), giving Black the initiative. This move leverages maximum board control and tempo.]\n\nAnswer: Q: e1-e5"}
